    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Policy on Political Expression in the Workplace\n\nTo the Leadership Team and All Employees,\n\nThis updated policy aims to strike a delicate balance between respecting individual freedom of thought and fostering a unified, professional environment essential for our high-impact tech operations.\n\nUnder **Incompatible Expressions**, specific actions will be prohibited if they create a hostile environment or serve as a pretext for discrimination; this includes the forced display of political gear on company property (such as lobbies) or using political affiliation to impede collaboration in cross-functional projects.\n\n**Communication Channels and Dress Code**\nRegarding internal tools like Slack and official email, political discussions must be contextualized to ensure clarity and relevance to work matters without diverting focus from business objectives.\nFor the **clothing and dress code**, political symbols or campaigns worn on personal time are permitted; however, if such items are worn on company gear (like laptops, swag, or mandatory safety-toe boots used for political messaging) or if they visibly divide the team in a shared workspace, they may be found disruptive to the culture we strive to maintain.\n\n**Defining the \"Line\"**\nThe core distinction lies in the *impact on the individual and the team*. \"Personal expression\" that",
