      "content": "thanks. you cut off at the end there. but i get what you're saying about the \"impact.\" \n\none thing though—in the slack section, you said political discussions should be \"contextualized\" to work matters. that seems a bit vague. if an employee posts something about a major social justice issue or a controversial law that they feel affects their identity, wouldn't that be considered \"relevant\" to their experience at work? \n\ndo you think the policy should prioritize protecting people from feeling uncomfortable or excluded, or should it prioritize protecting the right to voice those specific, controversial opinions? how do we decide which one is more important for the company?",
